    "title": "Tampa Renters Save Over $1,000 a Month as Mortgage Costs Outpace Rent - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Elizabeth Johanson ,\n1 days ago Renting a home in Tampa is now running about $1,100 cheaper per month than buying one, according to a new nationwide breakdown from Zillow that puts the Bay Area among dozens of major U.S. metros where the math clearly favors tenants over new homeowners. The gap is being driven by a familiar combination for Florida buyers: climbing mortgage rates, a flood of new apartment supply, and carrying costs — insurance and property taxes chief among them — that renters simply don't pay. Read full article",
